        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This elaborately embroidered purse probably corresponds to the \"sweet bags\" recorded in a number of sixteenth- and seventeenth-century inventories. The purse appears to have been worn around the person and to have carried scented herbs and essences to ward off the evil smells of daily life."@en ;
